# Scramble Generator Release Notes

## 1.17.1 (30 Jan 2025)

### New Features

- Initial release

### Improvements

- Added save config option and user defaults

### Bug Fixes

- Fixed initial setup issues

## 1.19.0 (24 Feb 2025)

### Improvements

- Removed save config option and user defaults
- Overhauled UI to make it more condensed and modern

## 1.20.0 (24 Feb 2025)

### Improvements

- Updated file structure to use `uv` instead of BeeWare

## 1.20.3 (20 Mar 2025)

### Bug Fixes

- Fixed custom module imports

### Improvements

- Removed unneeded variables
- Corrected variables that didn't need self-assignment

## 1.20.4 (31 Oct 2025)

### Improvements

- Reduced the required Python version

## 1.20.6 (21 Jul 2026)

### Improvements

- Version bump to update dependencies

## 1.20.21 (26 Oct 2026)

### Improvements

- Version bump to update dependencies and Python versions

## 2.0.0 (24 Nov 2026)

### New Features

- Added a Preferences dialog to manage default settings for puzzle type, move count, and auto-copy
- Added persistent settings using `QSettings` stored in `~/.config/scramble_generator/settings.conf`
- Added 12 new themes (Scramble Generator Dark/Light, Phaino Dark/Light, Equinox Dark/Light, Catppuccin Mocha/Latte, Solarized Dark/Light, Gruvbox Dark/Light) with live theme switching
- Added an About dialog accessible from the Help menu showing app version, author, and license
- Added a dynamic scrolling output area for long scrambles
- Added "Copy Scramble" and "Exit" actions to the menu bar

### Improvements

- Completely overhauled the GUI, replacing the fixed layout with a responsive card-based design
- Modularized the codebase, moving UI components into a flat `components/` directory
- Moved all styling into a centralized `styles.qss` file utilizing token substitution for dynamic theming
- Replaced hardcoded scramble generation logic with a programmatic approach that removes 150+ lines of dead code
- Removed `config.yaml` in favor of constants and `QSettings`

### Bug Fixes

- Fixed a bug where the `R5` move mapped to `R4'`
- Fixed the timer resetting to zero instead of stopping and showing the elapsed time
- Fixed the scramble output box clipping long scrambles
- Fixed the theme toggle logic being inverted
- Fixed the preferences dialog text being unreadable in dark mode
